  "note": "This is the availability our projections assume, reconciled from the official injury reports and our live feed \u2014 not injury news itself. \u201cQuestionable / day-to-day\u201d players still carry a real play chance; \u201cout\u201d players have their minutes redistributed. A row marked \u201cread from the latest report\u201d is one where our read is fresher than the raw feed status. Minutes next to an absence are that player's season average \u2014 the size of the role left to fill, from our player board. \u201cLikely to step up\u201d is the same depth-chart promotion our status board's game card flags \u2014 the player moved up the rotation the absence opened. An \u201cexpected back ~N games\u201d pill is a league-wide empirical guide \u2014 how long that injury TYPE has typically kept players out across 2023-25 (median, with a p25-p75 range) \u2014 not a player-specific prognosis; a thin or season-ending type falls back to the pooled baseline or an honest \u201cseason-ending\u201d instead of a made-up number.",
